    "https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF09906": {
      "title": "Recruit",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Scholar (JPF09906) - UCI - Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Postdoctoral Scholar (JPF09906) Postdoctoral Scholar Apply now to Postdoctoral Scholar Job #JPF09906 Medicine / School of Medicine / UC Irvine Position overview Salary range: Postdoctoral Series - All Levels A reasonable estimate for this position is $69,073-$82,836. Postdoctoral Scholar – Represented  Fiscal Year. Application Window Open date: September 24, 2025 Most recent review date: Tuesday, Nov 25, 2025 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications received after this date will be reviewed by the search committee if the position has not yet been filled. Final date: Thursday, Sep 24, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description A postdoctoral position is available at the University of California, Irvine in the laboratory of Dr. Mehboob Hussain. The successful candidate will explore regulation of metabolism in multiple tissues using in in vivo mouse models as well as human (stem) cell systems and tissues to examine metabolism regulation and disease pathogenesis and amply bioinformatic tools to identify and experimentally test novel inter-tissue signaling pathways that regulate metabolic homeostasis and/or cause disease Our lab employs cutting-edge approaches and state-of-the-art technologies. UC Irvine is a world-class research university with highly ranked graduate programs in biomedical sciences. Our Southern California location is home to one of the largest academic research and biotechnology hubs in the US. Lab members enjoy direct access to this outstanding community of clinicians and scientists, as well as the wide range of recreational activities available in our region. Successful candidates will join an interdisciplinary and highly collaborative team working to develop the next generation of tools and technologies to advance precision diagnostics and therapeutics. Essential Skills • Applicant can have their PhD at the time of the application or could be working towards the PhD or MD/PhD degree with a focus on Metabolism, Mouse Models systems, Human stem cell systems, Biochemical and Molecular Tools, Epigenetics, Genetics, Genomics, Biology, Bioinformatics, Machine Learning, or a related field • Extensive experience in a research environment and at least 1 first-author publication in a reputable scientific journal. The candidate is expected to have a record of academic accomplishments, including contributions to published or in-press research in the field The candidate should have past expertise in working with a colony of genetically modified mouse models (incl. genotyping) and be proficient in working with cell culture systems,  and general laboratory biochemical and molecular biological techniques (including but not limited to: ELISA, Immunohistochemistry and confocal microscopy, immunoblotting, RNA extractions, RT-qPCR . The candidate is expected to be familiar with standard software (MS Office Suite, Adobe Suite, Statistical and Graph Software packages i.e. Graphpad Prism) • Ability to work independently to drive projects forward • Ability to communicate effectively and collaborate as part of a multidisciplinary team • Ability to compose and deliver comprehensive presentations at scientific meetings and prepare research articles for peer-reviewed publications Additional Qualifications • Experience in In vivo metabolic characterization of mouse models, • Experience in isolation and culture of metabolic relevant tissues (ie isolated islets, isolated liver cells, adipose tissue),  small rodent surgeries (e.g. miniosmotic pump implantation into mice), •Experience in stem cell differentiation protocols in to metabolic relevant cell-types • Experience in next generation molecular biological tools e.g. next generation sequencing, Chip-Seq, Cut&Tag , preparation of libraries for sequencing and downstream bioinformatic analysis of data sets Ideal Skills • Experience in In vivo metabolic characterization of mouse models. • Experience in isolation and culture of metabolic relevant tissues (ie isolated islets, isolated liver cells, adipose tissue),  small rodent surgeries (e.g. miniosmotic pump implantation into mice), • Experience in next generation molecular biological tools e.g. next generation sequencing, Chip-Seq, Cut&Tag , preparation of libraries for sequencing and downstream bioinformatic analysis of data sets • Experience with sectioning, fixing, and staining tissues for histology imaging, laser capture microdissection, and sample prep for (single-cell) sequencing. • Expertise with ATAC-Seq, methylation profiling, genome/exome/targeted sequencing, mutation calling, single-cell analysis, RNA-Seq, proteomics, spatial technologies from 10X, NanoString or similar, cryoET or cryoEM analysis. •  Experience in biocomputational methods and be willing to engage in  methods to analyze data and further develop additional expertise in this area •  Experience  in at least 1 programming language and machine learning models. Ideally, candidates will also have some familiarity with basic biology, next-generation sequencing data, and statistical modelling of high-dimensional datasets. Experience in basic computational methods (e.g. R, Python, and/or other programming languages) • Experience in developing computational analysis pipelines • Experience with building highly distributable software (e.g., R packages, Python modules, Linux-based command-line tools, C programs, MATLAB applications, GitHub) The candidate will further support all laboratory activities including managing laboratory operations, participating in new protocol development, mouse protocol applications, supervision of students, assistance in mentoring trainees, preparation of grant applications as well as publications, participating in laboratory meetings and in collaborations with other laboratories. Ideally the candidate will pursue an independent project within the scope of the laboratory's interest while overall supporting all laboratory operations. Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) Applicant can have their PhD at the time of the application or could be working towards the PhD or MD/PhD degree with a focus on Metabolism, Mouse Models systems, Human stem cell systems, Biochemical and Molecular Tools, Epigenetics, Genetics, Genomics, Biology, Bioinformatics, Machine Learning, or a related field Extensive experience in a research environment and at least 1 first-author publication in a reputable scientific journal. The candidate is expected to have a record of academic accomplishments, including contributions to published or in-press research in the field Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter (Optional) Statement of Research Reference requirements 3 required (contact information only) Apply link: https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF09906 About UC Irvine The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected categories covered by the UC anti-discrimination policy . As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct. “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment or discrimination, as defined by the employer. UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, Students and Third Parties APM - 035: Affirmative Action and Nondiscrimination in Employment . As a University employee, you will be required to comply with all applicable University policies and/or collective bargaining agreements, as may be amended from time to time. Federal, state, or local government directives may impose additional requirements. Job location Irvine, CA / Orange, CA Apply now to Postdoctoral Scholar or Log in to your portfolio Need help? Contact the hiring department . The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. You have the right to an equal employment opportunity . The University of California, Irvine is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities . See our Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act Annual Security Reports Academic Personnel Recruit University of California, Irvine UC Irvine Accessibility About California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Opt-Out Icon Privacy Policy © 2007-2026 The Regents of the University of California. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF09910": {
      "title": "Specialist Position",
      "description": "Specialist Position - Hochbaum Lab (JPF09910) - UCI - Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Specialist Position - Hochbaum Lab (JPF09910) Specialist Position - Hochbaum Lab Apply now to Specialist Position - Hochbaum Lab Job #JPF09910 Materials Science and Engineering / Henry Samueli School of Engineering / UC Irvine Position overview Salary range: The salary range for this position is $55,000--$194,800. Salary will be commensurate with experience. The posted UC salary scales set the minimum pay determined by rank and step at appointment. See Table [ https://drive.google.com/file/d/1QNifxBxLzwVT3Icr63X2YxPZ3aA58AWX/view ]. Application Window Open date: September 22, 2025 Most recent review date: Tuesday, Oct 21, 2025 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications received after this date will be reviewed by the search committee if the position has not yet been filled. Final date: Monday, Sep 21, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description Specialist Position – Hochbaum Lab 2025-2026 The Hochbaum research group in the UCI Samueli School of Engineering is anticipating an opening for a one-year appointment in the Specialist Series starting in the academic year 2025-2026. The position is associated with an industry-sponsored research project on the commercialization of a rapid antibiotic susceptibility testing diagnostic technology. The position will require strong teamwork skills, communication with colleagues in biomedical device engineering and medicine, the ability to organize and manage microbiological research within the lab, and the ability to plan and execute research activities to meet deadlines for deliverables. The position offers opportunities for networking within the biomedical technology industry. Seeking qualified candidates with research experience in basic microbial growth and characterization methods. Ideal candidates will have research experience in techniques to measure bacterial metabolism, viability, and antibiotic susceptibility. These positions require a B.S., M.S., or Ph.D. in Microbiology or related fields, and experience in the focus research area(s) listed above. This position is open for Specialists at all ranks—Junior, Assistant, Associate, and Full rank determined based on experience. This is an ongoing recruitment and positions are dependent upon availability of extramural funding. Initial appointments are short-term and renewal is based on job performance and availability of support. Salary is commensurate with qualifications and years of relevant experience. Application Procedure: Applicants will need to upload curriculum vitae, name/addresses of at least three references, cover letter expressing area(s) of interest and dates of availability to start the position to our online RECRUIT system at https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF09910 . Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) This position require a B.S., M.S., or Ph.D. in Microbiology or related fields Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter Statement of Research (Optional) Reflective Teaching and Mentoring Statement -   See our guidance for writing a reflective teaching statement . (Optional) Reference requirements 3 required (contact information only) Apply link: https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF09910 About UC Irvine The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected categories covered by the UC anti-discrimination policy . As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct. “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment or discrimination, as defined by the employer. UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, Students and Third Parties APM - 035: Affirmative Action and Nondiscrimination in Employment . As a University employee, you will be required to comply with all applicable University policies and/or collective bargaining agreements, as may be amended from time to time. Federal, state, or local government directives may impose additional requirements. Job location Irvine, CA Apply now to Specialist Position - Hochbaum Lab or Log in to your portfolio Need help? Contact the hiring department . The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. You have the right to an equal employment opportunity . The University of California, Irvine is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities . See our Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act Annual Security Reports Academic Personnel Recruit University of California, Irvine UC Irvine Accessibility About California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Opt-Out Icon Privacy Policy © 2007-2026 The Regents of the University of California. All rights reserved."
