      "description": "Health Sciences Clinical Professor Series - Family Medicine (JPF09962) - UCI - Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Health Sciences Clinical Professor Series - Family Medicine (JPF09962) Health Sciences Clinical Professor Series - Family Medicine Apply now to Health Sciences Clinical Professor Series - Family Medicine Job #JPF09962 Family Medicine / School of Medicine / UC Irvine Position overview Salary range: Total Negotiated Salary (TNS) calculation includes AAMC salary benchmarks for Family Medicine ranging from $237,500- $275,500. The posted UC salary scales set the base pay determined by rank and/or step at appointment. This position includes membership in the health science compensation plan , which provides for eligibility for additional compensation. Application Window Open date: December 1, 2025 Most recent review date: Thursday, Jan 1, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications received after this date will be reviewed by the search committee if the position has not yet been filled. Final date: Tuesday, Dec 1, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description JOB DESCRIPTION: The UC Irvine Department of Family Medicine anticipates openings for a full-time faculty position in the Department of Family Medicine, School of Medicine, at the University of California, Irvine. We are seeking qualified individuals who are excellent clinicians with a strong commitment to medical education. The position will be offered in the Health Sciences Clinical Professor Series at the Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor level. This position would have primary care practice at UCI's Federally Qualified Health Centers. DUTIES: Criteria for the Health Sciences Clinical Professor Series: The incumbent will be expected to provide patient care to an FQHC population and fulfill teaching and academic requirements for promotion. Teaching may include fellows, residents, and medical students during clinical activities as well as primary care related didactics. DESIRED SKILLS: Preference may be given to applicants who have the following skills: Spanish speaking, experience caring for underserved populations. REQUIREMENTS: M.D., D.O. or M.D./Ph.D./MPH. from an accredited institution with appropriate clinical training and experience. Have current or applied for California Medical License. Board-Certified in Family Medicine. Candidates must have demonstrated capabilities for teaching, professional service and/or research suitable to the HS Clinical Professor series. Positions are dependent upon funding. Salary and rank will be commensurate with qualifications and experience. Initial appointments are for one year and renewal is based on availability of support. TO APPLY: Please log onto UC Irvine’s RECRUIT located at https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF09962 • UCI is a Minority Serving Institution (MSI), a Hispanic-Serving Institution (HSI) and an Asian American and Native American Pacific Islander-Serving Institution (AANAPISI). These federal designations align with UCI as a national leader of inclusive excellence. • We seek faculty who are committed to diversity as well as diverse faculty who will be role models for students. Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) M.D., D.O. or M.D./Ph.D./MPH. from an accredited institution with appropriate clinical training and experience. Have current or applied for California Medical License. Board-Certified in Family Medicine. Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter Statement of Research (Optional) Teaching Statement -   See our guidance for writing a reflective teaching statement . Reference requirements 3 required (contact information only) Apply link: https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF09962 