    "https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10078": {
      "title": "Health Sciences Clinical Professor Series",
      "description": "Health Sciences Clinical Professor Series - Anesthesiology & Perioperative Care (JPF10078) - UCI - Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Health Sciences Clinical Professor Series - Anesthesiology & Perioperative Care (JPF10078) Health Sciences Clinical Professor Series - Anesthesiology & Perioperative Care Apply now to Health Sciences Clinical Professor Series - Anesthesiology & Perioperative Care Job #JPF10078 Anesthesiology / School of Medicine / UC Irvine Position overview Salary range: Total Negotiated Salary (TNS) depending on specialty can range from $440,000-$575,000.  The posted UC salary scales set the minimum pay determined by rank and/or step at appointment.  This position includes membership in the health science compensation plan , which provides for eligibility for additional compensation. Application Window Open date: July 2, 2026 Next review date: Thursday, Sep 17, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Apply by this date to ensure full consideration by the committee. Final date: Wednesday, Jun 30, 2027 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description UC Irvine School of Medicine Department of Anesthesiology & Perioperative Care Health Sciences Clinical Professor Series The Department of Anesthesiology & Perioperative Care at the University of California, Irvine anticipates openings for physicians in general anesthesia and its various divisions. These openings will be at the level of Assistant Professor or above, depending upon the candidate’s qualifications and will be in the Health Sciences Clinical Series (non-tenure track).  Candidate must be board eligible or board certified. Candidate must be eligible for California licensure or licensed to practice in the state of California.  Fellowship trained or equivalent experience preferred. Criteria for the Professor in the HS Series: Health Sciences Clinical Professor Series faculty engage in scholarly or creative activities which derive from and support their primary responsibilities in clinical teaching and professional and service activities. The divisions include Cardiac, Critical Care, Neonatal/Pediatrics, Neuro, Obstetrics, Pain Medicine, and Regional. The Health Sciences Clinical Professor will provide care at UCI Medical Center in Orange, CA and Irvine, CA and/or affiliated sites in Orange County. Clinicians interested in pursuing an academic career in Anesthesiology and related specialties will be given the opportunity to grow in a dynamic department. There are ample opportunities for leadership roles, research, and career advancement. Our team includes a group of innovative, forward-thinking individuals with high standards of teaching, research, and patient care. Job duties include but are not limited to: • Perioperative Management: Including, but not limited to the assessment, examination and optimization of the surgical patient. • General Anesthesiology: Including but not limited to inhalational anesthetics, intravenous anesthetics and use of muscle relaxants. • Monitored Anesthesia Care • Airway management: Including but not limited to Ventilation using bag and mask, laryngoscopy and intubation, laryngeal mask airway, fiberoptic laryngoscopy and intubation, bronchoscopy, cricothyroidotomy and other difficult airway techniques. • Conduction/Regional Anesthesia: Including but not limited to Epidural Analgesia/ Anesthesia, Spinal Anesthesia, IV regional blocks (bier block), infiltration blocks, plexus blocks with and without catheter placement (brachial, supraclavicular, lumbo-sacral), peripheral nerve and field blocks, epidural blocks (caudal, lumbar, thoracic), and subarachnoid blocks using nerve stimulation or ultrasound. • Placement and use of invasive hemodynamic monitoring including arterial cannulation, central venous cannulation, pulmonary artery catheter placement. • Routine surface ultrasonography for line placement and surface diagnostics. • Mechanical ventilation to accomplish physiologic homeostasis. • Obstetric Anesthesia: Placement and management of labor epidurals and continuous spinal epidurals, management of conduction and general anesthesia for caesarian section, and neonatal resuscitation. • Cardiopulmonary resuscitation • Supervision and care of patients in the post-anesthesia care unit. • Management of acute pain in patients. • Anesthetic management of common pediatric anesthesia cases in children 2 to 16 years of age. • Pain Management: Including, but not limited to initial consultations, longitudinal management, opioid management, performing and managing sympathetic blocks, spinal injections, radiofrequency ablation, trigger point injections, joint injections, differential nerve blocks, botulinum toxin injections, spinal cord stimulation and intrathecal pump delivery system therapies. UCI Medical Center in Orange is a 459-bed acute care hospital equipped with state-of-the-art operating rooms and is the region’s only Level I trauma center and Level II pediatric trauma center. It is the primary teaching and training location for the UCI School of Medicine. For 21 consecutive years, the medical center has been rated among America’s Best Hospitals by U.S. News & World Report. UCI Health recently built and opened in 2025, UCI Medical Center-Irvine, a full-service academic health complex that will bring a broad spectrum of the most advanced healthcare services.  The medical campus, which complements the flagship UCI Medical Center in Orange, includes a seven-story, 144-bed general acute care hospital with a 24-hour emergency department. It also features the Chao Family Comprehensive Cancer Center and Ambulatory Care building and the Joe C. Wen & Family Center for Advanced Care . UCI offers an excellent salary, incentive, and benefit program . Faculty rank and compensation is commensurate with experience and qualifications. The Health Sciences Clinical Professor Series faculty will have on average a 40-hour work week clinical commitment including call responsibilities. Applicants are required to be board certified/eligible and licensed to practice in the state of California. Department : http://www.anesthesiology.uci.edu/ School : https://www.som.uci.edu/ Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) Candidate must hold a M.D. or M.D./Ph.D. degree(s) equivalent. Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Teaching Statement -   See our guidance for writing a reflective teaching statement . Teaching Evaluations -   Please provide recent (within the past 5 years) individual teaching evaluations and profile of statistical teaching summaries. If there are no teaching evaluations submitted with the application, provide an explanation within your teaching statement and upload the document. Reference requirements 5 required (contact information only) Apply link: https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10078 About UC Irvine The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected categories covered by the UC anti-discrimination policy . As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct. “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment or discrimination, as defined by the employer. UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, Students and Third Parties APM - 035: Affirmative Action and Nondiscrimination in Employment . As a University employee, you will be required to comply with all applicable University policies and/or collective bargaining agreements, as may be amended from time to time. Federal, state, or local government directives may impose additional requirements. Job location Orange, CA / Irvine, CA Apply now to Health Sciences Clinical Professor Series - Anesthesiology & Perioperative Care or Log in to your portfolio Need help? Contact the hiring department . The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. You have the right to an equal employment opportunity . The University of California, Irvine is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities . See our Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act Annual Security Reports Academic Personnel Recruit University of California, Irvine UC Irvine Accessibility About California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Opt-Out Icon Privacy Policy © 2007-2026 The Regents of the University of California. All rights reserved."
