    "https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10133": {
      "title": "2026/27 Psychology Lecturer Pool AdApply nowto 2026/27 Psychology Lecturer Pool Ad",
      "description": "2026/27 Psychology Lecturer Pool Ad (JPF10133) - UCI - Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments 2026/27 Psychology Lecturer Pool Ad (JPF10133) 2026/27 Psychology Lecturer Pool Ad Apply now to 2026/27 Psychology Lecturer Pool Ad Job #JPF10133 Psychology / School of Social Ecology / UC Irvine Position overview Salary range: A reasonable estimate for this position is based on an annual salary of $70,977. See NON-SENATE INSTRUCTIONAL UNIT 18 for the salary range for this position. Application Window Open date: May 6, 2026 Most recent review date: Monday, Jun 8, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications received after this date will be reviewed by the search committee if the position has not yet been filled. Final date: Monday, Feb 1, 2027 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description The Department of Psychology anticipates openings for Lecturers during fall quarter 2026, winter quarter 2027, and spring quarter 2027. These appointments will be made as the need arises to cover specific topics in the areas of developmental, social, personality, health, biological, clinical, and cultural psychology, as well as in research methods and statistics. Appointments will generally be for one quarter, but can be made for up to two or three quarters. The salary is commensurate with experience, at varying percentages of time depending on the course(s) assigned. The Department of Psychology at UCI offers exciting and innovative programs of study at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Our faculty members are prominent scholars whose specialties include developmental, social, personality, health, biological, clinical, and cultural psychology, as well as psychology and law. The faculty are united by an overarching interest in understanding the origins of human behavior as it develops across the life course and in diverse sociocultural contexts. The faculty also share a strong commitment to interdisciplinary scholarship and to research that has the potential for application to important societal problems. Appointments vary based on need and availability. The service period for the academic year, three quarters: 2026-2027 7/1/26-6/30/27 Fall 2026 Service Dates: 09/21/26 to 12/11/26 Pay Period 9/12: 07/01/26 to 10/31/26 Pay Period 9/9: 10/01/26 to 12/31/26 Winter 2027 Service Dates: 01/04/27 to 03/19/27 Pay Period 9/12: 11/01/26 to 02/28/27 Pay Period 9/9: 01/01/27 to 03/31/27 Spring 2027 Service Dates: 03/24/27 to 06/11/27 Pay Period 9/12: 03/01/27 to 06/30/27 Pay Period 9/9: 04/01/27 to 06/30/27 Requirements – Master's degree with a preferred Ph.D/doctoral degree in psychology or a related field Interested applicants should submit the required documents via UC Irvine’s online application system, RECRUIT. Department : https://ps.soceco.uci.edu/ Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) Master's degree or higher in psychology or a related field Teaching experience at the college level Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter (Optional) Statement of Research (Optional) Teaching Statement -   See our guidance for writing a reflective teaching statement . (Optional) Reference requirements 3 required (contact information only) Names and contact information only.  Please do not solicit letters. Apply link: https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10133 About UC Irvine The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected categories covered by the UC anti-discrimination policy . As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct. “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment or discrimination, as defined by the employer. UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, Students and Third Parties APM - 035: Affirmative Action and Nondiscrimination in Employment . As a University employee, you will be required to comply with all applicable University policies and/or collective bargaining agreements, as may be amended from time to time. Federal, state, or local government directives may impose additional requirements. Job location Irvine, CA Apply now to 2026/27 Psychology Lecturer Pool Ad or Log in to your portfolio Need help? Contact the hiring department . The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. You have the right to an equal employment opportunity . The University of California, Irvine is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities . See our Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act Annual Security Reports Academic Personnel Recruit University of California, Irvine UC Irvine Accessibility About California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Opt-Out Icon Privacy Policy © 2007-2026 The Regents of the University of California. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10134": {
      "title": "In-Residence Professor Series – Geriatric Medicine (JPF10134)",
      "description": "In-Residence Professor Series – Geriatric Medicine (JPF10134) - UCI - Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments In-Residence Professor Series – Geriatric Medicine (JPF10134) In-Residence Professor Series – Geriatric Medicine Apply now to In-Residence Professor Series – Geriatric Medicine Job #JPF10134 Family Medicine / School of Medicine / UC Irvine Position overview Salary range: Total Negotiated Salary (TNS) calculation includes AAMC salary benchmarks for this position is ranging from $237,500- $275,500. The posted UC salary scales set the base pay determined by rank and/or step at appointment. This position includes membership in the health science compensation plan , which provides for eligibility for additional compensation. Application Window Open date: July 6, 2026 Most recent review date: Monday, Aug 31, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications received after this date will be reviewed by the search committee if the position has not yet been filled. Final date: Tuesday, Jul 6, 2027 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description The University of California, Irvine (UCI) School of Medicine, Division of Geriatric Medicine and Gerontology is seeking Family Medicine/Internal Medicine/Preventive Medicine candidates for a full-time faculty position as an Assistant Professor, Associate Professor or Professor (level depending on experience) for an In-Residence position. The Division is housed in the department of Family Medicine. The division of Geriatric Medicine and Gerontology is home to faculty, fellows, and staff who have a passion for patient care, medical education, research and community health. Our mission, as a department in the UCI School of Medicine, is to Discover, Teach, Heal and Serve. We are committed to delivering exemplary clinical care, teaching health professionals and research to promote health and well-being for older adults. Our division includes Family Medicine and Internal Medicine physicians, advanced practice providers, and psychologists, comprising a team-based approach to Geriatric medicine, as well as researchers and dedicated staff. Geriatricians provide care in many environments including UCI Health’s Orange SeniorHealth Center, Laguna Hills specialty care, Irvine’s Gottschalk Plaza, and affiliated skilled nursing facilities as well as home care. The Division has been awarded major grants and donor funds to improve the health of seniors through education, innovative clinical care and research. We offer an outstanding Geriatric Fellowship with three fellows annually. REQUIREMENTS: M.D., MD/PhD or D.O. from an accredited institution with appropriate clinical training and experience. Board certification in Family Medicine/ Internal Medicine/Preventive Medicine and strong interest in Geriatric Medicine; excellent clinical skills; interest in clinical teaching; eligibility for UC Irvine Medical Center medical staff privileges required. Candidate must have demonstrated capabilities for teaching, professional services and research suitable for the In-Residence series. PRACTICE INFORMATION: We are seeking an enthusiastic, caring physician to join an interdisciplinary outpatient practice at a UCI Health geriatric care site. The academic clinician will join the In-Residence faculty series with clinical care and research responsibilities. Our goal is to provide superb medical care for a diverse patient population. Outpatient practice is a teaching site for all levels of academic learners. This position includes a research role in collaboration with the UCI MIND center for Alzheimer disease and related dementia (ADRD) research. RESPONSIBILITIES: • Develop research linking clinical practice for older adults to research in dementia prevention and treatment. • Collaborate with faculty in the Schools of Medicine, Nursing, Pharmacy and Population Health, and MIND to develop interdisciplinary education. • Participate in local, national and international geriatric associations and organizations • Ambulatory patient care practice • Fellow supervision, residency teaching, and precepting medical students Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) M.D., MD/PhD or D.O. from an accredited institution with appropriate clinical training and experience Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter Statement of Research Teaching Statement -   See our guidance for writing a reflective teaching statement . Reference requirements 3 required (contact information only) Apply link: https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10134 About UC Irvine The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected categories covered by the UC anti-discrimination policy . As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct. “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment or discrimination, as defined by the employer. UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, Students and Third Parties APM - 035: Affirmative Action and Nondiscrimination in Employment . As a University employee, you will be required to comply with all applicable University policies and/or collective bargaining agreements, as may be amended from time to time. Federal, state, or local government directives may impose additional requirements. Job location Orange, California Apply now to In-Residence Professor Series – Geriatric Medicine or Log in to your portfolio Need help? Contact the hiring department . The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. You have the right to an equal employment opportunity . The University of California, Irvine is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities . See our Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act Annual Security Reports Academic Personnel Recruit University of California, Irvine UC Irvine Accessibility About California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Opt-Out Icon Privacy Policy © 2007-2026 The Regents of the University of California. All rights reserved."
