      "description": "Postdoctoral in Biomedical Imaging (Imaging Instrumentation) 2026-2027 (JPF10220) - UCI - Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Postdoctoral in Biomedical Imaging (Imaging Instrumentation) 2026-2027 (JPF10220) Postdoctoral in Biomedical Imaging (Imaging Instrumentation) 2026-2027 Apply now to Postdoctoral in Biomedical Imaging (Imaging Instrumentation) 2026-2027 Job #JPF10220 Radiological Sciences / School of Medicine / UC Irvine Position overview Salary range: The annual salary range for this position is $69,073-$82,836. See Postdoctoral Series Salary Scale Application Window Open date: July 1, 2026 Most recent review date: Sunday, Aug 30, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications received after this date will be reviewed by the search committee if the position has not yet been filled. Final date: Wednesday, Jun 30, 2027 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description The Department of Radiological Sciences at the University of California, Irvine, anticipates openings for a postdoctoral fellow in the TRUE Lab ( TRUE Lab ). We are seeking a creative, dedicated, and collaborative individual to join our interdisciplinary research team. Our lab focuses on cutting-edge radiacoustic imaging technologies for applications in cancer therapy and atrial fibrillation treatment. Minimum Qualifications: • PhD, MD, or MD/PhD in biomedical engineering, physics, electrical engineering, or a related field Preferred Qualifications: • Strong background in ultrasound imaging • Experience in photoacoustic imaging • Strong hands-on skills in medical device development or strong computational skills including signal processing and image reconstruction. School : https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10220 Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) • PhD, MD, or MD/