    "https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10222": {
      "title": "UCI Jr/Assistant Specialist",
      "description": "UCI Jr/Assistant Specialist - Department of Global Health and Biobehavioral Sciences (JPF10222) - UCI - Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments UCI Jr/Assistant Specialist - Department of Global Health and Biobehavioral Sciences (JPF10222) UCI Jr/Assistant Specialist - Department of Global Health and Biobehavioral Sciences Apply now to UCI Jr/Assistant Specialist - Department of Global Health and Biobehavioral Sciences Job #JPF10222 Global Health and Biobehavioral Sciences  / Joe C. Wen School of Population and Public Health / UC Irvine Position overview Salary range: The pay range for a Jr Specialist is between $55,000 - $70,700. Pay is determined by experience, please see chart: meaningful link text Application Window Open date: July 15, 2026 Most recent review date: Saturday, Aug 15, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications received after this date will be reviewed by the search committee if the position has not yet been filled. Final date: Wednesday, Sep 30, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description Position Description The Department of Global Health and Biobehavioral Sciences in the Joe C. Wen School of Population and Public Health at the University of California, Irvine (UCI) invites applications for a Junior Specialist or Associate Specialist position in the laboratory of Dr. Guiyun Yan. The Yan Laboratory conducts research in vector biology, vector-borne disease epidemiology, molecular genetics, and global health, with a particular focus on malaria and other mosquito-borne diseases. We seek a highly motivated and organized individual with strong laboratory, project management, and communication skills. Under the supervision of the Principal Investigator and senior laboratory personnel, the Junior Specialist will contribute to research activities, laboratory operations, and training initiatives that support ongoing federally funded research programs. Major Responsibilities • Assist with laboratory and field research activities related to disease vectors and vector-borne diseases. • Maintain laboratory operations, including ordering supplies, inventory management, equipment maintenance, organization, and compliance with laboratory safety procedures. • Prepare, update, and distribute laboratory protocols, standard operating procedures (SOPs), project reports, and research documentation. • Perform molecular, genetic, entomological, and epidemiological laboratory procedures. • Support mosquito vector and pathogen identification using standard laboratory methods. • Analyze, organize, and maintain research data and records. • Train and assist students, staff, and visiting researchers in laboratory techniques and protocols. • Participate in laboratory meetings and contribute to research presentations, reports, and publications as appropriate. • Perform other duties as assigned in support of the laboratory’s research mission. Application Instructions Applicants should apply through UC Irvine’s online recruitment system (AP Recruit). Applications should include: • Curriculum Vitae (CV) • Cover Letter • Three reference letters School : https://publichealth.uci.edu/ Department : https://publichealth.uci.edu/departments/global-health-biobehavioral-sciences/ Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) Required Qualifications: • Bachelor’s degree in Biological Sciences, Public Health, Molecular Biology, Entomology, Genetics, or a closely related field. • Experience working in a biological, molecular, or public health research laboratory. • Strong organizational, time-management, and interpersonal skills. • Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a fast-paced research environment. • Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Occasional evening and weekend work may be required based on research and project needs. Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter Reference requirements 3 required (contact information only) Apply link: https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10222 About UC Irvine The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected categories covered by the UC anti-discrimination policy . As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct. “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment or discrimination, as defined by the employer. UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, Students and Third Parties APM - 035: Affirmative Action and Nondiscrimination in Employment . As a University employee, you will be required to comply with all applicable University policies and/or collective bargaining agreements, as may be amended from time to time. Federal, state, or local government directives may impose additional requirements. Job location Irvine, CA Apply now to UCI Jr/Assistant Specialist - Department of Global Health and Biobehavioral Sciences or Log in to your portfolio Need help? Contact the hiring department . The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. You have the right to an equal employment opportunity . The University of California, Irvine is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities . See our Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act Annual Security Reports Academic Personnel Recruit University of California, Irvine UC Irvine Accessibility About California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Opt-Out Icon Privacy Policy © 2007-2026 The Regents of the University of California. All rights reserved."
