    "https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10237": {
      "title": "Health Sciences Clinical Professor Series, Urogynecology and Reconstructive Pelvic SurgeryApply nowto Health Sciences Clinical Professor Series, Urogynecology and Reconstructive Pelvic Surgery",
      "description": "Health Sciences Clinical Professor Series, Urogynecology and Reconstructive Pelvic Surgery (JPF10237) - UCI - Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Health Sciences Clinical Professor Series, Urogynecology and Reconstructive Pelvic Surgery (JPF10237) Health Sciences Clinical Professor Series, Urogynecology and Reconstructive Pelvic Surgery Apply now to Health Sciences Clinical Professor Series, Urogynecology and Reconstructive Pelvic Surgery Job #JPF10237 Obstetrics and Gynecology / School of Medicine / UC Irvine Position overview Salary range: The salary range for this position is $320,000 - $509,000. The posted UC salary scales set the minimum pay determined by rank and/or step at appointment. See Professorial Series (Adjunct, Clinical X, HS Clinical, In Residence, Ladder Rank) and Professor of Teaching Series – Health Sciences Compensation Plan . This position includes membership in the health sciences compensation plan , which provides for eligibility for additional compensation. Application Window Open date: July 16, 2026 Next review date: Wednesday, Sep 30, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Apply by this date to ensure full consideration by the committee. Final date: Wednesday, Jun 30, 2027 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology invites applications for a faculty position in the Health Sciences Clinical Series (non‑tenure track) at the level of Assistant Professor or higher, commensurate with qualifications. This position is within the Division of Urogynecology and Reconstructive Pelvic Surgery (URPS) and is dedicated to providing exceptional clinical and surgical care to our diverse patient population. The Division of URPS is a dedicated team of four board-certified URPS educators. We are proud of our nationally recognized three‑year integrated fellowship in partnership with Kaiser Permanente of Orange County. To promote our research mission, the division provides faculty with departmental statistical support, a director of research, clinical research coordinators, seed funding, and a regulatory coordinator. There are ample opportunities to collaborate with basic and translational scientists across multiple disciplines and departments. Responsibilities include private patient practice, supervision and teaching of medical students, residents, and fellows, engagement in scholarly activity, and participation in general faculty duties. We seek individuals who are enthusiastic about contributing to our fourfold mission to discover, teach, heal, and serve. Candidates must hold an MD or MD/PhD and possess a California medical license and Drug Enforcement Agency certificate by the start date. Applicants must be eligible for or certified by the American Board of Obstetrics and Gynecology and have completed accredited subspecialty training in Urogynecology and Reconstructive Pelvic Surgery, with subsequent specialty board candidacy or certification. Competitive candidates will demonstrate excellent clinical skills, strong medical knowledge, a commitment to teaching, and a record of scholarly achievement. The University of California, Irvine is a premier academic medical center located in the heart of Southern California. It is consistently ranked among the nation’s best hospitals in Gynecology by U.S. News & World Report. For more information about the Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology, please visit http://www.obgyn.uci.edu . Department : http://www.obgyn.uci.edu Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) Candidates must hold an MD or MD/PhD and possess a California medical license and Drug Enforcement Agency certificate by the start date. Applicants must be eligible for or certified by the American Board of Obstetrics and Gynecology and have completed accredited subspecialty training in Urogynecology and Reconstructive Pelvic Surgery, with subsequent specialty board candidacy or certification. Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter  -   Describe participation in research, patient care, performing university and public service, and demonstration of professional competency and activity. Teaching Statement -   See our guidance for writing a reflective teaching statement . Student/Teaching Evaluations -   Evaluations on teaching sessions, lectures, and/or presentations. Reference requirements 3 required (contact information only) Apply link: https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10237 About UC Irvine The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected categories covered by the UC anti-discrimination policy . As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct. “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment or discrimination, as defined by the employer. UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, Students and Third Parties APM - 035: Affirmative Action and Nondiscrimination in Employment . As a University employee, you will be required to comply with all applicable University policies and/or collective bargaining agreements, as may be amended from time to time. Federal, state, or local government directives may impose additional requirements. Job location Orange, CA Apply now to Health Sciences Clinical Professor Series, Urogynecology and Reconstructive Pelvic Surgery or Log in to your portfolio Need help? Contact the hiring department . The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. You have the right to an equal employment opportunity . The University of California, Irvine is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities . See our Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act Annual Security Reports Academic Personnel Recruit University of California, Irvine UC Irvine Accessibility About California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Opt-Out Icon Privacy Policy © 2007-2026 The Regents of the University of California. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10238": {
      "title": "Health Sciences Clinical Professor Series, General OB/GYN (JPF10238)",
      "description": "Health Sciences Clinical Professor Series, General OB/GYN (JPF10238) - UCI - Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Health Sciences Clinical Professor Series, General OB/GYN (JPF10238) Health Sciences Clinical Professor Series, General OB/GYN Apply now to Health Sciences Clinical Professor Series, General OB/GYN Job #JPF10238 Obstetrics and Gynecology / School of Medicine / UC Irvine Position overview Salary range: The salary range for this position is $280,000-$408,000. The posted UC salary scales set the minimum pay determined by rank and/or step at appointment. See Professorial Series (Adjunct, Clinical X, HS Clinical, In Residence, Ladder Rank) and Professor of Teaching Series – Health Sciences Compensation Plan . This position includes membership in the health sciences compensation plan , which provides for eligibility for additional compensation. Application Window Open date: July 16, 2026 Next review date: Wednesday, Sep 30, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Apply by this date to ensure full consideration by the committee. Final date: Wednesday, Jun 30, 2027 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description The Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology invites applications for a faculty position in the Health Sciences Clinical Series (non‑tenure track) at the level of Assistant Professor or higher, commensurate with qualifications. This position is within the Division of General Obstetrics and Gynecology and is dedicated to providing exceptional clinical and surgical care to our diverse patient population. The Division of General Obstetrics and Gynecology provides the full spectrum of Women’s Reproductive Health Care including low-risk obstetrics, ambulatory gynecology, and benign gynecologic surgery, as well as supervise residents and medical students in the only academic medical school in Orange County, California. Responsibilities include providing the full spectrum of obstetrical and gynecologic care within the UCI faculty practice, including GYN inpatient care, along with dedicated time supervising resident continuity clinics at UCI’s Federally Qualified Health Centers. The role also involves supervising and teaching trainees at all levels, participating in scholarly activities, and maintaining a private patient practice. Additional duties include educating medical students, residents, and fellows. We seek individuals who are enthusiastic about contributing to our fourfold mission to discover, teach, heal, and serve. Candidates must hold an MD or equivalent, possess a California medical license and Drug Enforcement Agency certificate by the start date, and be eligible for or certified by the American Board of Obstetrics and Gynecology. Candidates should also have excellent clinical skills, medical knowledge, interest in teaching, and scholarly accomplishments, as well as possess a strong interest in serving the diverse populations in our community. For more information about the Department of Obstetrics and Gynecology, please visit http://www.obgyn.uci.edu Department : http://www.obgyn.uci.edu Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) Candidates must hold an MD or equivalent, possess a California medical license and Drug Enforcement Agency certificate by the start date, and be eligible for or certified by the American Board of Obstetrics and Gynecology. Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter -   Describe participation in research, patient care, performing university and public service, and demonstration of professional competency and activity. Student/Teaching Evaluations -   Evaluations on teaching sessions, lectures, and/or presentations. Statement of Teaching -   See our guidance for writing a reflective teaching statement . Reference requirements 3 required (contact information only) Apply link: https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10238 About UC Irvine The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected categories covered by the UC anti-discrimination policy . As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct. “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment or discrimination, as defined by the employer. UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, Students and Third Parties APM - 035: Affirmative Action and Nondiscrimination in Employment . As a University employee, you will be required to comply with all applicable University policies and/or collective bargaining agreements, as may be amended from time to time. Federal, state, or local government directives may impose additional requirements. Job location Orange, CA Apply now to Health Sciences Clinical Professor Series, General OB/GYN or Log in to your portfolio Need help? Contact the hiring department . The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. You have the right to an equal employment opportunity . The University of California, Irvine is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities . See our Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act Annual Se