    "https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10250": {
      "title": "Math FellowApply nowto Math Fellow",
      "description": "Math Fellow (JPF10250) - UCI - Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Math Fellow (JPF10250) Math Fellow Apply now to Math Fellow Job #JPF10250 Mathematics / School of Physical Sciences / UC Irvine Position overview Salary range: The full-time annual salary for this position starts at $74,600. Application Window Open date: August 18, 2026 Next review date: Sunday, Jan 31, 2027 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Apply by this date to ensure full consideration by the committee. Final date: Wednesday, Jun 30, 2027 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description Applications are invited for Math Fellows, subject to renewal for up to three years, in all areas of mathematics. Any Post Doc experience prior to starting at UCI will count towards the overall Math Fellow experience and may effect the amount of years available for renewal.  For example, if your postdoc candidate has 3 years of postdoc experience at another university, the maximum they will be able to serve as a Math Fellow at UCI is 2 years.  Math Fellows teach no more than five quarter classes per year. Strong promise in research and teaching is required. Appointments will be effective July 1, 2027, or later. Applicants must possess a Ph.D. in Mathematics or related field by employment start date. Completed applications must be submitted through AP Recruitment Link - Math Fellow and must contain: (1) Cover letter (2) CV (3) Research statement (4) Teaching statement - See our guidance for writing a reflective teaching statement: Teaching Statement Guide (5) Teaching (TA) evaluations (6) Selected reprints and/or preprints (7) Three reference letters (at least one addressing teaching) (8) Sexual Misconduct, Harassment and Discrimination Declaration Form Please reference job #10250 in the subject line of all correspondence. Applications are welcome at any time. The review process starts September 2026 and will continue until positions are filled. Department : https://www.math.uci.edu/ Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) A PhD degree in mathematics or a related field by appointment start and a good teaching record is preferred, but applicants with similar education or work experience will be considered. Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter Teaching Evaluations Teaching Statement -   See our guidance for writing a reflective teaching statement . Statement of Research -   Please upload a required Statement of Research. Reference requirements 3-5 letters of reference required Apply link: https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10250 About UC Irvine The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected categories covered by the UC anti-discrimination policy . As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct. “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment or discrimination, as defined by the employer. UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, Students and Third Parties APM - 035: Affirmative Action and Nondiscrimination in Employment . As a University employee, you will be required to comply with all applicable University policies and/or collective bargaining agreements, as may be amended from time to time. Federal, state, or local government directives may impose additional requirements. Job location Irvine, CA Apply now to Math Fellow or Log in to your portfolio Need help? Contact the hiring department . The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. You have the right to an equal employment opportunity . The University of California, Irvine is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities . See our Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act Annual Security Reports Academic Personnel Recruit University of California, Irvine UC Irvine Accessibility About California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Opt-Out Icon Privacy Policy © 2007-2026 The Regents of the University of California. All rights reserved."
