    "https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10255": {
      "title": "UCI Associate Specialist/ Full Specialist",
      "description": "UCI Associate Specialist/ Full Specialist - Department of Health, Society, and Behavior (JPF10255) - UCI - Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments UCI Associate Specialist/ Full Specialist - Department of Health, Society, and Behavior (JPF10255) UCI Associate Specialist/ Full Specialist - Department of Health, Society, and Behavior Apply now to UCI Associate Specialist/ Full Specialist - Department of Health, Society, and Behavior Job #JPF10255 Health, Society and Behavior / Joe C. Wen School of Population and Public Health / UC Irvine Position overview Salary range: Pay for this position varies and depends on experience, pay scale between $75,600 -$165,200. Please see table: meaningful link text Application Window Open date: July 24, 2026 Most recent review date: Monday, Aug 24, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications received after this date will be reviewed by the search committee if the position has not yet been filled. Final date: Thursday, Oct 1, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description Dr. Brandy Lipton is seeking applications for an Associate Specialist/Specialist to join the Department of Health, Society, and Behavior within the University of California, Irvine’s Department of Health, Society, and Behavior. The Specialist would work closely with Dr. Lipton on a variety of projects that examine the effects of public policies on population health and well-being using quasi-experimental research methods. This position is funded by grants from the National Institutes of Health. Background: The Specialist will be expected to contribute to research examining the impacts of state-level Medicaid policies using a variety of survey and administrative data sources (e.g., Medicaid claims data). Candidates for this position should have experience in working with large datasets including data cleaning, coding, and statistical analysis. There will be opportunities to collaborate on manuscripts intended for publication in high-impact policy, economics, and medical journals. Remote work is possible and negotiable, but some in-person presence is strongly preferred. Specific Duties: -Assist with data cleaning, coding, and statistical analysis in Stata or other statistical programs using large micro-level and population-level datasets. -Perform bivariate and multivariate analyses -Prepare tables of descriptive statistics and publication-quality figures -Attend regular project meetings and effectively communicate statistical results -Contribute to grant and manuscript development -Contribute to applications for restricted datasets -Contribute to Institutional Review Board protocols -Assist in compiling and analyzing state-level policies, including conducting searches on the WestLaw legal database -Work closely with junior student team members to improve research products -Provide citation management, proofreading, code review, and presentation development on an as-needed basis Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) Required Qualifications: -Master’s degree in economics, Health Policy, Public Policy, Public Health -Project management skills -Strong quantitative data analysis skills -Fluency in Stata, SAS, Python, or R Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter (Optional) Statement of Research (Optional) Reference requirements 3 required (contact information only) Apply link: https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10255 About UC Irvine The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected categories covered by the UC anti-discrimination policy . As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct. “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment or discrimination, as defined by the employer. UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, Students and Third Parties APM - 035: Affirmative Action and Nondiscrimination in Employment . As a University employee, you will be required to comply with all applicable University policies and/or collective bargaining agreements, as may be amended from time to time. Federal, state, or local government directives may impose additional requirements. Job location Irvine, CA Apply now to UCI Associate Specialist/ Full Specialist - Department of Health, Society, and Behavior or Log in to your portfolio Need help? Contact the hiring department . The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. You have the right to an equal employment opportunity . The University of California, Irvine is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities . See our Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act Annual Security Reports Academic Personnel Recruit University of California, Irvine UC Irvine Accessibility About California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Opt-Out Icon Privacy Policy © 2007-2026 The Regents of the University of California. All rights reserved."
