      "title": "Specialist Series, Open Ranks, Beckman Laser Institute (JPF10265)",
      "description": "Specialist Series, Open Ranks, Beckman Laser Institute (JPF10265) - UCI - Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Specialist Series, Open Ranks, Beckman Laser Institute (JPF10265) Specialist Series, Open Ranks, Beckman Laser Institute Apply now to Specialist Series, Open Ranks, Beckman Laser Institute Job #JPF10265 Beckman Laser Institute and Medical Clinic / School of Medicine / UC Irvine Position overview Salary range: The salary range for this position is $57,000-$201,700. The posted UC salary scales set the minimum pay determined by rank and step at appointment. meaningful link text Application Window Open date: July 2, 2026 Most recent review date: Saturday, Aug 1, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications received after this date will be reviewed by the search committee if the position has not yet been filled. Final date: Wednesday, Jun 30, 2027 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description The Beckman Laser Institute at the University of California, Irvine  seeks applicants with an interest in translational optical imaging. Responsibilities include image collection analysis and computer-based instrumentation. Experience in biophotonics and LabView and MATLAB programming desirable. Candidates should have a Bachelor's degree preferably in Physics, Chemistry, or Optical Engineering. Candidates must have the ability to work in an interdisciplinary setting. Experience in biophotonics and LabView and MATLAB programming desirable. Requirements: Candidates must have the ability to work in an interdisciplinary setting. All appointments are for one year with the potential for extension dependent upon performance and funding. TO APPLY: Please log onto UC Irvine’s RECRUIT located at Browse Open Recruitments or Log In - UCI - Recruit Department : http://www.bli.uci.edu/specialist/ Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) Junior Specialist - Appointees to the Junior rank should possess a baccalaureate degree (or equivalent degree) or equivalent research experience. Assistant Specialists -Appointees to the Assistant rank should possess a master’s degree (or equivalent degree), or five years of experience demonstrating expertise in the relevant specialization. Associate Specialist - should possess a master’s degree (or equivalent degree) or five to ten years of experience demonstrating expertise in the relevant specialization. Associate Specialists are normally expected to have a record of academic accomplishments, including contributions to published or inpress research in the field and a demonstrated record of University and/or public service. Specialist - should possess a terminal degree (or equivalent degree) or ten or more years of experience demonstrating expertise in the relevant specialization. Specialists at full rank are normally expected to have a significant record of academic accomplishments, including contributions to published or in-press research in the field, professional recognition in the field, and a demonstrated record of University and/or public service. Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter (Optional) Statement of Research (Optional) Reference requirements 3 required (contact information only) Apply link: https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10265 About UC Irvine The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected categories covered by the UC anti-discrimination policy . As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any 