    "https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10316": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Public Budgeting & Financial Management (JPF10316)",
      "description": "Lecturer in Public Budgeting & Financial Management (JPF10316) - UCI - Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Lecturer in Public Budgeting & Financial Management (JPF10316) Lecturer in Public Budgeting & Financial Management Apply now to Lecturer in Public Budgeting & Financial Management Job #JPF10316 Urban Planning and Public Policy / School of Social Ecology / UC Irvine Position overview Salary range: Starting at $70,977 Review timeline: Applications received by Aug. 16, 2026 will receive priority review. Application Window Open date: July 30, 2026 Most recent review date: Sunday, Aug 30, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications received after this date will be reviewed by the search committee if the position has not yet been filled. Final date: Thursday, Dec 31, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description The Department of Urban Planning and Public Policy in the School of Social Ecology invites applications for a qualified lecturer to teach a course in Public Budgeting and Financial Management for its online Master of Public Administration. The course will be offered in Spring Quarter 2027. In addition to teaching responsibilities, general duties include preparing course materials for asynchronous online instruction (syllabus, recorded lectures, assignments, etc.), maintaining a course website, holding office hours, assigning grades, and advising students. To assist with course development, the lecturer will have access to a team of instructional designers through the Social Ecology Hub for Innovative Education. Required: M.A., M.S. or doctoral students who are advanced to candidacy in a field appropriate to the course (e.g., Public Administration, Urban Planning, Public Policy). Desired: A Ph.D. in a field appropriate to the course (e.g., Public 