    "https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10332": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Film and Media Industry Studies (JPF10332)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Film and Media Industry Studies (JPF10332) - UCI - Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Assistant Professor of Film and Media Industry Studies (JPF10332) Assistant Professor of Film and Media Industry Studies Apply now to Assistant Professor of Film and Media Industry Studies Job #JPF10332 Film and Media Studies / School of Humanities / UC Irvine Position overview Salary range: The salary range for this position is $93,500 - 121,400. The posted UC salary scales set the minimum pay determined by rank and/or step at appointment. See Professor and Professor of Teaching Series – Academic Year Regular Scales. “Off-scale salaries” and other components of pay, i.e., a salary that is higher than the published system-wide salary at the designated rank and step, are offered when necessary to meet competitive conditions. Review timeline: Review of applications will begin November 1, 2026 and continue until the position is filled (start date is July 1, 2027). Applications completed by November 1, 2026 will be granted full consideration. Application Window Open date: August 4, 2026 Next review date: Sunday, Nov 1, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Apply by this date to ensure full consideration by the committee. Final date: Tuesday, Dec 1, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description The Department of Film and Media Studies at the University of California, Irvine invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Film and Media Industry Studies to begin July 1, 2027. We welcome applications from scholars conducting historical and/or contemporary research and specializing in film, television, streaming, video games, social media, and/or other media industries. We conceive industry studies broadly to include production studies, policy studies, political economy, labor studies, and infrastructure studies. Candidates who study any geographic region are welcome to apply, and we especially welcome candidates who explore inter/transnational media industries or media industries of the Global South. Applicants must demonstrate potential for excellence in scholarship, as well as in teaching a range of core and elective courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels, graduate mentoring, and university service. Ph.D. in Film and Media Studies or related field is required; degrees must be completed by June 30, 2027. To apply, please upload your cover letter, CV, article-length writing sample, names and contact information for three references, and reflective teaching statement via UC Irvine’s on-line application system, AP Recruit . Additional materials, such as letters of recommendation and sample syllabi, may be requested by the search committee at a later date. Review of applications will begin November 1, 2026 and continue until the position is filled (start date is July 1, 2027). Applications completed by November 1, 2026 will be granted full consideration. UC Irvine is a leading public research institution and part of the University of California system. UC Irvine offers B.A. and Ph.D. degrees in Film and Media Studies. UC Irvine is a minority-thriving campus . Candidates are welcome to discuss any work related to inclusive excellence in their written materials. A reflective teaching statement should: Indicate the candidate’s teaching experiences to date, including experience with teaching undergraduates/graduate students, or other populations, as well as their areas of interest. This should also include mentorship that they have given to others in the line of research or outreach activities. Detail the candidate’s teaching approaches and philosophies, as to how they will engage in effective teaching strategies. For additional information, please contact Amy Fujitani , Department Manager. Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) Ph.D. in Film and Media Studies or related field is required. Applicants must demonstrate potential for excellence in scholarship, as well as in teaching a range of core and elective courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels, graduate mentoring, and university service. Degree must be completed by June 30, 2027. Application Requirements Document requirements Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Writing Sample -   Upload an article-length writing sample. Reflective Teaching Statement -   See our guidance for writing a reflective teaching statement . Reference requirements 3 required (contact information only) Letters of recommendation may be requested by the search committee at a later date. Apply link: https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10332 About UC Irvine The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected categories covered by the UC anti-discrimination policy . As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct. “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment or discrimination, as defined by the employer. UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, Students and Third Parties APM - 035: Affirmative Action and Nondiscrimination in Employment . As a University employee, you will be required to comply with all applicable University policies and/or collective bargaining agreements, as may be amended from time to time. Federal, state, or local government directives may impose additional requirements. Job location Irvine, CA Apply now to Assistant Professor of Film and Media Industry Studies or Log in to your portfolio Need help? Contact the hiring department . The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. You have the right to an equal employment opportunity . The University of California, Irvine is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities . See our Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act Annual Security Reports Academic Personnel Recruit University of California, Irvine UC Irvine Accessibility About California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Opt-Out Icon Privacy Policy © 2007-2026 The Regents of the University of California. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10334": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Psychology – Quantitative, Computational, and Data Science (JPF10334)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Psychology – Quantitative, Computational, and Data Science (JPF10334) - UCI - Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Assistant Professor, Psychology – Quantitative, Computational, and Data Science (JPF10334) Assistant Professor, Psychology – Quantitative, Computational, and Data Science Apply now to Assistant Professor, Psychology – Quantitative, Computational, and Data Science Job #JPF10334 Psychology / School of Social Ecology / UC Irvine Position overview Salary range: The salary range for this position is $80,800- $104,700. The posted UC salary scales set the minimum pay determined by rank and/or step at appointment. See Professor and Professor of Teaching Series – Academic Year Regular Scales . “Off-scale salaries” and other components of pay, i.e., a salary that is higher than the published system-wide salary at the designated rank and step, are offered when necessary to meet competitive conditions. Application Window Open date: August 5, 2026 Next review date: Sunday, Nov 15, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Apply by this date to ensure full consideration by the committee. Final date: Thursday, Dec 31, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description The Department of Psychology at the University of California, Irvine, invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant Professor level. The Department of Psychology seeks to expand its expertise in quantitative, computational, and data science approaches to understanding human behavior and psychological processes. Scholars in this area may develop or apply advanced methods, including machine learning and artificial intelligence, computational modeling, causal inference, epidemiologic methods, advanced statistical modeling, natural language processing, network analysis, and other data science approaches, to address complex psychological questions. Their research may leverage large-scale, population-based, intensive longitudinal, multimodal, or digitally-generated behavioral data, including text, social interaction, smartphones and sensors, administrative and clinical records, cohort and registry data, and other emerging sources of human behavioral data. Scholars’ expertise needs to fit into one of the Department’s existing substantive areas of developmental, health, social, or clinical psychology. Candidates must have a doctoral degree in psychology or a closely related discipline. The position will begin July 1, 2027, with teaching duties beginning Fall Quarter, 2027. Applications must be uploaded electronically through the on-line Recruit system Please direct questions about this position to the chair of the search committee, Professor Stephen Schueller . Visit the Department of Psychology website Visit the UCI School of Social Ecology website Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) Candidates must have a doctoral degree in psychology or a closely related discipline. Application Requirements Document requirements Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Statement of Research Reflective Teaching and Mentoring Statement -   See our guidance for writing a reflective teaching statement . Reference requirements 3 required (contact information only) Apply link: https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10334 About UC Irvine The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected categories covered by the UC anti-discrimination policy . As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct. “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment or discrimination, as defined by the employer. UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, Students and Third Parties APM - 035: Affirmative Action and Nondiscrimination in Employment . As a University employee, you will be required to comply with all applicable University policies and/or collective bargaining agreements, as may be amended from time to time. Federal, state, or local government directives may impose additional requirements. Job location Irvine, CA Apply now to Assistant Professor, Psychology – Quantitative, Computational, and Data Science or Log in to your portfolio Need help? Contact the hiring department . The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. You have the right to an equal employment opportunity . The University of California, Irvine is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities . See our Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act Annual Security Reports Academic Personnel Recruit University of California, Irvine UC Irvine Accessibility About California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Opt-Out Icon Privacy Policy © 2007-2026 The Regents of the University of California. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10335": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Health PsychologyApply nowto Assistant Professor, Health Psychology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Health Psychology (JPF10335) - UCI - Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Assistant Professor, Health Psychology (JPF10335) Assistant Professor, Health Psychology Apply now to Assistant Professor, Health Psychology Job #JPF10335 Psychology / School of Social Ecology / UC Irvine Position overview Salary range: The salary range for this position is $80,800- $104,700 . The posted UC salary scales set the minimum pay determined by rank and/or step at appointment. See Professor and Professor of Teaching Series – Academic Year Regular Scales . “Off-scale salaries” and other components of pay, i.e., a salary that is higher than the published system-wide salary at the designated rank and step, are offered when necessary to meet competitive conditions. Application Window Open date: August 11, 2026 Next review date: Sunday, Nov 1, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Apply by this date to ensure full consideration by the committee. Final date: Thursday, Dec 31, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description The Department of Psychology at the University of California, Irvine invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant Professor level in health psychology with an anticipated start date of July 1, 2027 (teaching duties will begin Fall 2027). We seek a scholar with strong training in health psychology and closely related areas whose research examines the psychological, social, behavioral, cognitive, and/or biological processes that shape physical health and well-being. We are particularly interested in candidates studying stress, resilience, and health; social and emotional influences on health; psychophysiological or biopsychosocial pathways; health behavior and behavior change; psychological contributors to health disparities; and/or interventions designed to improve health and well-being. Research may address these questions at any point or across multiple periods of the lifespan. The successful candidate will have a theoretically grounded and methodologically rigorous research program that contributes to the core discipline of health psychology. We welcome a range of methodological approaches, including laboratory experiments, longitudinal and intensive repeated-measures designs, psychophysiological and other biological assessments, ambulatory and digital measurement, intervention research, and population-based approaches. We are especially interested in candidates whose work integrates multiple levels of analysis and complements the department’s social ecological approach to understanding health and human behavior. Although candidates may draw upon social, clinical, developmental, affective, or neuroscience perspectives, the position is intended to strengthen the department’s core research and teaching capacity in health psychology. The successful candidate will be expected to teach foundational undergraduate and graduate courses in health psychology, contribute additional courses in their area of expertise, mentor students, and maintain an active program of research with strong potential for external funding. The Department of Psychology values collaborative and interdisciplinary scholarship. Faculty have opportunities to collaborate across the School of Social Ecology and with researchers throughout UC Irvine, including those in public health, medicine, nursing, biological sciences, and related fields and centers (e.g., the Center for Biomarker & Biobehavioral Research). The department is especially interested in scholars whose research will contribute to its strengths in understanding how psychological processes and social contexts influence physical and psychological health. To ensure full consideration, applications should be completed by November 1, 2026. Applications received by that date will receive priority; however, applications may be accepted until the position is filled. Applications must be submitted electronically through the UC Irvine Recruit System Candidates should submit: A cover letter describing their interest in the position A curriculum vitae A statement of research A statement of teaching Three representative publications or other scholarly works Names and contact information for three professional references Please direct questions about the position to Professor Sarah Pressman, chair of the search committee, at pressman@uci.edu . Visit the Department of Psychology website Visit the School of Social Ecology website Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) Applicants must hold a doctoral degree in psychology by the time of appointment. Candidates who have not yet completed the doctoral degree at the time of application must provide evidence that the degree will be completed before the position’s anticipated start date. Application Requirements Document requirements Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Statement of Research Reflective Teaching  Statement -   See our guidance for writing a reflective teaching statement . Three representative publications or other scholarly works Reference requirements 3 required (contact information only) Applicants must provide the names and contact information for three professional references. Letters of recommendation will be requested only for candidates who advance to the later stages of review. References for selected candidates should be prepared to submit letters promptly upon request. Apply link: https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10335 About UC Irvine The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected categories covered by the UC anti-discrimination policy . As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct. “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment or discrimination, as defined by the employer. UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, Students and Third Parties APM - 035: Affirmative Action and Nondiscrimination in Employment . As a University employee, you will be required to comply with all applicable University policies and/or collective bargaining agreements, as may be amended from time to time. Federal, state, or local government directives may impose additional requirements. Job location Irvine, CA Apply now to Assistant Professor, Health Psychology or Log in to your portfolio Need help? Contact the hiring department . The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. You have the right to an equal employment opportunity . The University of California, Irvine is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities . See our Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act Annual Security Reports Academic Personnel Recruit University of California, Irvine UC Irvine Accessibility About California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Opt-Out Icon Privacy Policy © 2007-2026 The Regents of the University of California. All rights reserved."
