    "https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10361": {
      "title": "Recruit",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Scholar - Climate, Pollution, and Solutions (JPF10361) - UCI - Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Postdoctoral Scholar - Climate, Pollution, and Solutions (JPF10361) Postdoctoral Scholar - Climate, Pollution, and Solutions Apply now to Postdoctoral Scholar - Climate, Pollution, and Solutions Job #JPF10361 Earth System Science / School of Physical Sciences / UC Irvine Position overview Salary range: $69,073 - $82,836 Application Window Open date: August 10, 2026 Next review date: Thursday, Sep 10, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Apply by this date to ensure full consideration by the committee. Final date: Monday, Nov 30, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description The Department of Earth System Science at the University of California, Irvine is seeking a postdoctoral scholar to work on rapid response modeling of air quality and health impacts of energy policy. This position is within the Climate, Pollution, and Solutions group led by Professor Lyssa Freese, and is in collaboration with a network of university researchers and environmental organizations. Start dates are flexible over Fall 2026-Spring 2027 time period (with preference for earlier start dates). Position benefits and pay: This is a two to three-year position that is renewable, pending good progress and funding. The salary will range from $69,073 to $82,836 USD per year, scaling with experience as detailed in the Postdoc Salary Scale , and includes excellent benefits via the Postdoctoral Scholar Benefit Plan – UCI Postdoctoral Association Project/Position description: Responsibilities will include development work on air pollution/atmospheric chemistry models, running and interpreting results from models, pairing air pollution models with integrated assessment or other energy system/policy oriented models, and interpreting data and results. Postdoctoral scholars are expected to lead peer-reviewed scientific publications, present at relevant conferences, and engage with policy oriented outputs such as policy briefs and white papers. You will be joining an interdisciplinary, multi-institutional team of researchers on this project, including researchers from universities and environmental organizations, so participation in collaborative research and interdisciplinary meetings and discussions is key to the project. Perks of the ESS department and UCI Campus: The Earth System Science Department at UC Irvine is highly interdisciplinary. It includes 25 faculty with broad expertise, all devoted to the study of the Earth as a coupled system. UC Irvine is located in Orange County, about halfway between the diverse metropolitan areas of Los Angeles and San Diego. It is a sunny and pleasant place to live, surrounded by beaches, parks, mountains. Our group is part of CLEWS (Climate, Land, Energy, and Water Solutions) and AirUCI, allowing for collaboration and interaction with atmospheric chemists, climate scientists, and civil/environmental engineers. We also have external relationships and collaborations with public health scientists, economists, and energy system modelers. If you have questions, you can reach out to Prof. Freese ( lyssa.freese@uci.edu ), with the subject line “Postdoc Application Question”. Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) ● An expected or recent Ph.D. in atmospheric sciences, atmospheric chemistry, environmental engineering or relevant interdisciplinary fields ● Proficient in programming ● Experience in computational modeling and working with high performance computing ● Experience working with atmospheric chemistry and/or air pollution models, such as chemical transport models, plume models, or reduced form models ● Demonstrated effective written and verbal communication skills Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   A curriculum vitae including publications list, Cover Letter -   A cover letter that also describes your immediate and long-term research goals Statement of Research (Optional) Teaching Statement -   See our guidance for writing a reflective teaching statement . (Optional) Reference requirements 3-5 required (contact information only) Apply link: https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10361 About UC Irvine The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected categories covered by the UC anti-discrimination policy . As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct. “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment or discrimination, as defined by the employer. UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, Students and Third Parties APM - 035: Affirmative Action and Nondiscrimination in Employment . As a University employee, you will be required to comply with all applicable University policies and/or collective bargaining agreements, as may be amended from time to time. Federal, state, or local government directives may impose additional requirements. Job location Irvine, CA Apply now to Postdoctoral Scholar - Climate, Pollution, and Solutions or Log in to your portfolio Need help? Contact the hiring department . The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. You have the right to an equal employment opportunity . The University of California, Irvine is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities . See our Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act Annual Security Reports Academic Personnel Recruit University of California, Irvine UC Irvine Accessibility About California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Opt-Out Icon Privacy Policy © 2007-2026 The Regents of the University of California. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10362": {
      "title": "Recruit",
      "description": "Eddleman Quantum Institute 2026 Postdoctoral Fellowship (JPF10362) - UCI - Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Eddleman Quantum Institute 2026 Postdoctoral Fellowship (JPF10362) Eddleman Quantum Institute 2026 Postdoctoral Fellowship Apply now to Eddleman Quantum Institute 2026 Postdoctoral Fellowship Job #JPF10362 Physics and Astronomy / School of Physical Sciences / UC Irvine Position overview Salary range: EQI Postdoctoral Fellows will receive an annual stipend of $80,000 with benefits as well as travel support and relocation assistance. Application Window Open date: September 1, 2026 Next review date: Sunday, Nov 1, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Apply by this date to ensure full consideration by the committee. Final date: Wednesday, Jun 30, 2027 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description The Eddleman Quantum Institute (EQI) at the University of California, Irvine (UCI), invites applications for the EQI Postdoctoral Fellowship from researchers with demonstrated accomplishments in quantum science and exceptional promise as future leaders in the field. Made possible by a gift from Roy Eddleman, this two-year fellowship aims to advance quantum research and foster collaborations across EQI and UCI. Outstanding candidates from all EQI research areas are encouraged to apply. This year, the fellowship is prioritized for experimentalist candidates. Applicants must be co-sponsored by at least two EQI faculty members. A list of the EQI Faculty and their research areas can be found at the website: Eddleman Quantum Institute . Applicants must contact potential EQI faculty sponsors before the application deadline to discuss research plans and collaboration opportunities. The fellowship provides for full salary and benefits as well as travel support and relocation costs. Fellows are supported for two years with a start date beginning in 2027. The EQI Postdoctoral Fellow is expected to contribute to the development of collaborative research in their areas and to engage in EQI educational and outreach activities. The application must include: (1) A current CV with a publication list (2) A research plan that outlines the collaborative research project of the Applicant and at least two EQI co-sponsors (3 page maximum, including figures and references) (3) The names and contact information for two reference writers who can comment on the applicant’s research accomplishments and independence. (4) The names of two UCI EQI faculty who have agreed to co-sponsor the applicant. The EQI Postdoctoral Fellowship will be awarded on the basis of the applicant's research accomplishments, independence, quality of the research plan, impact on EQI collaborations, and alignment with EQI’s goals. The goals of EQI are to stimulate the discovery of new quantum phenomena and train future generations of quantum scientists. EQI includes faculty from the UCI Departments of Physics and Astronomy, Chemistry, Mathematics, Computer Science, Materials Science and Engineering, and Electrical Engineering and Computer Science. Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) Candidates must possess or be in the progress of attaining a Ph.D. in Physics, Chemistry, Mathematics, Electrical Engineering, Materials Science, Computer Science, or another field related to quantum science. Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae  -   Your most recently updated C.V. and Publication list Statement of Research -   A brief summary of the applicant’s most significant research accomplishments and a collaborative research proposal involving the Applicant and at least two EQI co-sponsors (3 page maximum). List the names of the EQI co-sponsors at the top of the statement. A joint letter from the UCI EQI co-sponsors -   This letter will be submitted by the UCI EQI faculty co-sponsors upon the review of the application file. (Optional) Reference requirements 2-5 letters of reference required Apply link: https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10362 About UC Irvine The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected categories covered by the UC anti-discrimination policy . As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct. “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment or discrimination, as defined by the employer. UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, Students and Third Parties APM - 035: Affirmative Action and Nondiscrimination in Employment . As a University employee, you will be required to comply with all applicable University policies and/or collective bargaining agreements, as may be amended from time to time. Federal, state, or local government directives may impose additional requirements. Job location Irvine, CA Apply now to Eddleman Quantum Institute 2026 Postdoctoral Fellowship or Log in to your portfolio Need help? Contact the hiring department . The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. You have the right to an equal employment opportunity . The University of California, Irvine is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities . See our Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act Annual Security Reports Academic Personnel Recruit University of California, Irvine UC Irvine Accessibility About California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Opt-Out Icon Privacy Policy © 2007-2026 The Regents of the University of California. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10367": {
      "title": "Recruit",
      "description": "Visiting Scholar (JPF10367) - UCI - Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Visiting Scholar (JPF10367) Visiting Scholar Apply now to Visiting Scholar Job #JPF10367 Psychology / School of Social Ecology / UC Irvine Position overview Salary range: This is a without salary (WOS) position. The visitor will receive a cost-of-living allowance of $10,000, calculated at $1,000 per week for 10 weeks, to be disbursed monthly in arrears. Application Window Open date: July 30, 2026 Most recent review date: Wednesday, Sep 2, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications received after this date will be reviewed by the search committee if the position has not yet been filled. Final date: Thursday, Oct 1, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description UC Irvine’s Center for Psychology and Law welcomes scholars from outside institutions to contribute to its academic community. UC Irvine’s Center for Psychology and law serves as a hub for research that connects the fields of psychology and law. Its mission is to foster collaboration among academics, legal professionals, policymakers, and the public to address real-world issues where social sciences intersect with legal systems. The center aims to translate scientific evidence into public policy and practice, enhancing the understanding of psychological principles in legal contexts. A Visiting Scholar appointment is designed for independent researchers who are on leave from an academic position or other professional employment to conduct collaborative or independent research at UC Irvine. To be eligible, you must meet the following criteria: • Degree Status: You must hold a Ph.D. or the highest terminal degree in your field, typically earned more than five years ago. • Employment Status: Per University of California policy, you must be actively employed or hold an academic position elsewhere and be on official leave during your visit. • Location: All research activities must be conducted in person on the UC Irvine campus. Remote appointments are not permitted. • Duration: Appointment will be for winter quarter 2027 (01/04/2027 – 03/12/2027). • Cost-of-living allowance: The visitor will receive a cost-of-living allowance of $10,000, calculated at $1,000 per week for 10 weeks, to be disbursed monthly in arrears. • Housing: Furnished apartments may be available (depending on vacancies) on campus for the visiting scholar. Furnished Apartment Rates & Eligibility - Irvine Campus Housing Authority • UC System Restriction: Current UC faculty, staff, postdoctoral scholars, and students (across all UC campuses) are ineligible for this title due to existing UC reciprocity agreements. Additionally, Visiting Scholars cannot hold concurrent UC employment or paid appointments (such as a Lecturer position to teach a course) during their visit. Key Responsibilities: The visiting scholar will conduct independent or collaborative research in the field of Psychology and the Law, and present findings, deliverables, or publications resulting from the visit. The scholar will be expected to engage with UC Irvine faculty, students, and other researchers to promote academic exchange. They also must maintain a professional presence on campus, including attending Center for Psychology and Law events and departmental activities. During their appointment, Visiting Scholars are expected to present a talk highlighting their research to the UC Irvine community and conduct a half-day seminar for graduate students in the Department. Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) Ph.D. or the highest terminal degree in your field, typically earned more than five years ago. Per University of California policy, you must be actively employed or hold an academic position elsewhere and be on official leave during your visit. Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter Reference requirements 2 required (contact information only) Apply link: https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10367 About UC Irvine The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected categories covered by the UC anti-discrimination policy . As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct. “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment or discrimination, as defined by the employer. UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, Students and Third Parties APM - 035: Affirmative Action and Nondiscrimination in Employment . As a University employee, you will be required to comply with all applicable University policies and/or collective bargaining agreements, as may be amended from time to time. Federal, state, or local government directives may impose additional requirements. Job location Irvine, CA Apply now to Visiting Scholar or Log in to your portfolio Need help? Contact the hiring department . The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. You have the right to an equal employment opportunity . The University of California, Irvine is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities . See our Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act Annual Security Reports Academic Personnel Recruit University of California, Irvine UC Irvine Accessibility About California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Opt-Out Icon Privacy Policy © 2007-2026 The Regents of the University of California. All rights reserved."
