    "https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10376": {
      "title": "Lecturer Pool Ad",
      "description": "Lecturer Pool Ad - Physics and Astronomy (JPF10376) - UCI - Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Lecturer Pool Ad - Physics and Astronomy (JPF10376) Lecturer Pool Ad - Physics and Astronomy Apply now to Lecturer Pool Ad - Physics and Astronomy Job #JPF10376 Physics and Astronomy / School of Physical Sciences / UC Irvine Position overview Salary range: $73,817  - $90,786 Application Window Open date: September 4, 2026 Next review date: Saturday, Oct 3, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Apply by this date to ensure full consideration by the committee. Final date: Wednesday, Jun 30, 2027 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description The Department of Physics and Astronomy anticipates possible temporary positions for Lecturers for the 2026-2027 academic year. These positions usually become available as unexpected needs arise shortly before the start of a quarter. Positions are generally for one quarter at a time and are at varying percentages, depending on the number and nature of courses assigned. Applicants must possess a Ph.D., and have a good teaching record. Appointments may be effective (Fall Quarter) October 1, 2026~ (Winter Quarter) January 1, 2027 (Spring Quarter) April 1, 2027. Completed applications must be submitted electronically through https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/apply/JPF10376 and must contain: (1) Cover Letter (2) CV (3) Teaching Statement (4) Scanned copies of teaching evaluations (5) Three reference letters submitted through https://recruit.ap.uci.edu Please reference JPF#10376 in the subject line of all correspondence. Applications are welcome at any time. The review process is ongoing, and will continue until positions are filled. Applications received by September 1st will be given priority, but the position will remain open until filled. Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) Candidates must possess a Ph.D. or equivalent in Physics or a related field. Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter Statement of Research (Optional) Teaching Statement -   See our guidance for writing a reflective teaching statement . Reference requirements 3-5 letters of reference required Apply link: https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10376 About UC Irvine The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected categories covered by the UC anti-discrimination policy . As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct. “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment or discrimination, as defined by the employer. UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, Students and Third Parties APM - 035: Affirmative Action and Nondiscrimination in Employment . As a University employee, you will be required to comply with all applicable University policies and/or collective bargaining agreements, as may be amended from time to time. Federal, state, or local government directives may impose additional requirements. Job location Irvine, CA Apply now to Lecturer Pool Ad - Physics and Astronomy or Log in to your portfolio Need help? Contact the hiring department . The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. You have the right to an equal employment opportunity . The University of California, Irvine is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities . See our Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act Annual Security Reports Academic Personnel Recruit University of California, Irvine UC Irvine Accessibility About California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Opt-Out Icon Privacy Policy © 2007-2026 The Regents of the University of California. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10377": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Systems BiologyApply nowto Assistant Professor in Systems Biology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor in Systems Biology (JPF10377) - UCI - Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Assistant Professor in Systems Biology (JPF10377) Assistant Professor in Systems Biology Apply now to Assistant Professor in Systems Biology Job #JPF10377 Systems Biology / Charlie Dunlop School of Biological Sciences / UC Irvine Position overview Salary range: The salary range for this position is $93,500-$121,400. The posted UC salary scales set the minimum pay determined by rank and/or step at appointment. See Professor and Professor of Teaching Series – Academic Year Regular Scales .  “Off-scale salaries” and other components of pay, i.e., a salary that is higher than the published system-wide salary at the designated rank and step, are offered when necessary to meet competitive conditions. Application Window Open date: September 1, 2026 Next review date: Thursday, Oct 1, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Apply by this date to ensure full consideration by the committee. Final date: Saturday, Oct 31, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description UCI invites applications for a full-time tenure-track Assistant Professor position to join the faculty of the newly formed Department of Systems Biology in the Charlie Dunlop School of Biological Sciences at the University of California, Irvine. Systems Biology seeks to address unmet needs in the biological sciences at all levels of analysis, from molecules to species. It focuses on the understanding of biological networks and complexity, leveraging theory, models, experimentation, data science and AI.  As it is a highly interdisciplinary field, qualified candidates may have backgrounds in mathematics, physics, engineering, computer science or any biological subdiscipline, but are expected to have demonstrated a commitment to Systems Biology approaches in their research. Applicants should hold a Ph.D., M.D.-Ph.D., or equivalent degree(s) and demonstrate evidence of a rigorous research program based on prior research productivity and future research plans. Applicants are expected to contribute to teaching at both the graduate and undergraduate levels and demonstrate a commitment to service and leadership at UCI and wider communities. Please submit a curriculum vitae, 3-page description of research interests and accomplishments, 1-page statement of teaching and mentoring experience, and the contact details for three referees. Information on the department is available at: Systems Biology | UC Irvine Charlie Dunlop School of Biological Sciences The successful candidate will be able to leverage and complement existing strengths of the Department of Systems Biology, as well as the larger Mathematical, Computational and Systems Biology research communities, as represented by the UCI Center for Complex Biological Systems . A recipient of an NSF ADVANCE award for gender equity, UCI is responsive to the needs of dual career couples, supports work-life balance through an array of family-friendly policies, and is dedicated to broadening participation in higher education. UCI is a Minority Serving Institution (MSI), a Hispanic-Serving Institution (HSI) and an Asian American and Native American Pacific Islander-Serving Institution (AANAPISI). These federal designations align with UCI’s aspiration to be a national leader and global model of inclusive excellence. We seek faculty who are committed to promoting diversity, as well as diverse faculty who will be role models for our students. Department : https://systems.bio.uci.edu/ Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) Applicants should hold a Ph.D., M.D.-Ph.D., or equivalent degree(s). Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter Statement of Research -   An overview of prior and ongoing research and an outlook for future research directions to establish independence (3 pages). Reflective Teaching and Mentoring Statement -   This statement should indicate the candidate’s teaching experiences to date, and their areas of teaching interest. In addition to didactic teaching experiences, applicants may also describe research mentorship experiences, outreach activities, and other related experiences and plans. Candidates should describe their teaching approach and philosophy, active and evidence-based teaching strategies, or other plans for engaging in effective teaching strategies. If possible, provide evidence of effectiveness of previous teaching. See our guidance for writing a reflective teaching statement (1 page). Reference requirements 3 required (contact information only) Please only provide contact information with the application submission.  Letter requests will be sent for candidates under serious consideration after initial application review by the committee. Apply link: https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10377 About UC Irvine The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected categories covered by the UC anti-discrimination policy . As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct. “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment or discrimination, as defined by the employer. UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, Students and Third Parties APM - 035: Affirmative Action and Nondiscrimination in Employment . As a University employee, you will be required to comply with all applicable University policies and/or collective bargaining agreements, as may be amended from time to time. Federal, state, or local government directives may impose additional requirements. Job location Irvine, CA Apply now to Assistant Professor in Systems Biology or Log in to your portfolio Need help? Contact the hiring department . The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. You have the right to an equal employment opportunity . The University of California, Irvine is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities . See our Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act Annual Security Reports Academic Personnel Recruit University of California, Irvine UC Irvine Accessibility About California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Opt-Out Icon Privacy Policy © 2007-2026 The Regents of the University of California. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10379": {
      "title": "Recruit",
      "description": "Academic Emergency Medicine Physician (Health Sciences Series Open ranks, Pool Ad) (JPF10379) - UCI - Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Academic Emergency Medicine Physician (Health Sciences Series Open ranks, Pool Ad) (JPF10379) Academic Emergency Medicine Physician (Health Sciences Series Open ranks, Pool Ad) Apply now to Academic Emergency Medicine Physician (Health Sciences Series Open ranks, Pool Ad) Job #JPF10379 Emergency Medicine / School of Medicine / UC Irvine Position overview Salary range: The salary range for this position is $315,964-$406,183. The posted UC salary scales set the minimum pay determined by rank and step at appointment. See Table(s) . This position may include membership in the health sciences compensation plan , which provides for eligibility for additional compensation. Application Window Open date: August 21, 2026 Next review date: Monday, Sep 28, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Apply by this date to ensure full consideration by the committee. Final date: Wednesday, Jun 30, 2027 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description The University of California, Irvine (UCI) Department of Emergency Medicine is now accepting applications from skilled physician educators who are passionate about advancing clinical care, education and research within a fast-pace, high-volume, clinical/academic setting. Positions are available in the Health Sciences Clinical Professor series, at the Assistant, Associate or Full Professor rank. Candidates must possess a DO, MD or MD/PhD and board certification /board eligibility in Emergency Medicine. California DEA registration, California Medical License/ California Medical License eligibility and the ability to obtain California UCIMC staff credentials are required. Strong interest and demonstrated abilities in delivering patient care in an academic clinical setting, teaching residents and medical students, and providing service to the University are required. Those with post-doctoral trainings, fellowships, sub-specializations and/or advanced degrees/certifications are strongly desired. The incumbent will be expected to teach fellows, residents, medical students and other academic learners, provide quality patient care, collaborate on research and/or creative works and perform university and public service. Demonstrated evidence of capabilities for excellent teaching and creative works suitable for the series is expected. Positions are dependent upon funding. Rank and salary will be commensurate with training, qualifications, and experience. Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) DO, MD or MD, PhD Application Requirements Document requirements You are very welcome to discuss in your materials how your past activities and ongoing plans contribute to your ability to address the needs of all the communities of California you will be serving, including those historically underrepresented in higher education. Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter Teaching Statement -   See our guidance for writing a reflective teaching statement . Reference requirements 3 required (contact information only) Apply link: https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10379 About UC Irvine The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected categories covered by the UC anti-discrimination policy . As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct. “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment or discrimination, as defined by the employer. UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, Students and Third Parties APM - 035: Affirmative Action and Nondiscrimination in Employment . As a University employee, you will be required to comply with all applicable University policies and/or collective bargaining agreements, as may be amended from time to time. Federal, state, or local government directives may impose additional requirements. Job location Orange, CA. or Irvine, CA. Apply now to Academic Emergency Medicine Physician (Health Sciences Series Open ranks, Pool Ad) or Log in to your portfolio Need help? Contact the hiring department . The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. You have the right to an equal employment opportunity . The University of California, Irvine is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities . See our Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act Annual Security Reports Academic Personnel Recruit University of California, Irvine UC Irvine Accessibility About California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Opt-Out Icon Privacy Policy © 2007-2026 The Regents of the University of California. All rights reserved."
