    "https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10408": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Tenure-Track) Position in Quantum and Semiconductor Engineering (JPF10408)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (Tenure-Track) Position in Quantum and Semiconductor Engineering (JPF10408) - UCI - Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Assistant Professor (Tenure-Track) Position in Quantum and Semiconductor Engineering (JPF10408) Assistant Professor (Tenure-Track) Position in Quantum and Semiconductor Engineering Apply now to Assistant Professor (Tenure-Track) Position in Quantum and Semiconductor Engineering Job #JPF10408 Electrical Engineering and Computer Science / Henry Samueli School of Engineering / UC Irvine Position overview Salary range: The salary range for this position is $111,400-$241,400. The posted UC salary scales set the minimum pay determined by rank and/or step at appointment. See Professor and Professor of Teaching Series – Academic Year Regular Scales. “Off-scale salaries” and other components of pay, i.e., a salary that is higher than the published system-wide salary at the designated rank and step, are offered when necessary to meet competitive conditions. See Salary Scale Application Window Open date: September 4, 2026 Next review date: Tuesday, Dec 1, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Apply by this date to ensure full consideration by the committee. Final date: Monday, Feb 15, 2027 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description The Nhữ Department of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science (EECS) at the University of California, Irvine invites applications for an Assistant Professor (Tenure-Track) position in Quantum and Semiconductor Engineering, with an anticipated start in July 2027. Advances in quantum computing, sensing, and communications increasingly hinge on engineered semiconductor platforms, heterogeneous integration, and the device/circuit infrastructure that connects quantum hardware to scalable systems. The new position will complement and strengthen the department’s broader growth areas, including electromagnetics (photonics, RF, and microwave systems), quantum devices, III-V semiconductors, nanotechnology, and hardware-software integrated systems. The department seeks candidates who will build a high-visibility, externally funded research program at the intersection of quantum technologies and semiconductor engineering and catalyze collaborations spanning devices, circuits, photonics, electromagnetics, communications, computer engineering, and adjacent disciplines. Applicants with expertise across experimental, computational, and theoretical approaches are welcome. Strong fits include research that advances scalable quantum platforms and the enabling device/circuit stack, such as qubit-electronics co-design; cryo-CMOS and cryogenic RF control/readout hardware; III-V quantum electronics; superconducting, spin, photonic, or atomic implementations; hybrid quantum-microsystem integration and cross-domain transduction; quantum technology, sensing and communication; and heterogeneous integration and advanced packaging strategies that translate laboratory demonstrations into robust, manufacturable, and deployable quantum technologies. The position is expected to strengthen campus-scale initiatives and shared research infrastructure, including active engagement with the UCI Eddleman Quantum Institute, the Integrated Nanosystems Research Facility (INRF), and the UCI Irvine Materials Research Institute (IMRI). The successful candidate will help position EECS for multi-investigator center-scale proposals and major collaborative efforts aligned with federal critical and emerging technology priorities in quantum information science and semiconductors. In addition to building a strong independent program, the new faculty member will be encouraged to link UCI’s strengths in materials, nanofabrication, photonics, RF/microwaves, communication and computing into integrated quantum and semiconductor research directions. As a central component, the position requires teaching and developing undergraduate and graduate courses in areas such as quantum engineering, semiconductor devices, nanofabrication, microelectronics, and/or photonics, and is expected to incorporate hands-on laboratory experiences where appropriate. Bridging research and curriculum, the successful candidate will train students to work across quantum-classical interfaces and prepare graduates to lead in next-generation quantum and semiconductor technology industries. Applicants should hold a Ph.D. in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Applied Physics, or a closely related field by the start date. Applications should be submitted electronically at ( Browse Open Recruitments or Log In - UCI - Recruit ). The screening will begin immediately upon receipt of a completed application. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled, although maximum consideration will be given to applications received by December 1, 2026. UCI is a member of the Association of American Universities (AAU), is ranked as a top ten public university by U.S. News and World Report and was identified by the New York Times as number one among U.S. universities that do the most for low-income students. UCI is a Minority Serving Institution (MSI), a Hispanic-Serving Institution (HSI) and an Asian American and Native American Pacific Islander-Serving Institution (AANAPISI). These federal designations align with UCI’s aspiration to be a national leader and global model of inclusive excellence.  We seek faculty who are committed to serving as role models for our students who come from a wide variety of backgrounds, cultures, and beliefs. Information about the department is available at: ( Samueli School of Engineering at UC Irvine | EngineeringPlus ) Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) Applicants are expected to have a doctoral degree in Electrical Engineering, Computer Science, or a related field from an accredited university. Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter Statement of Research Reflective Teaching and Mentoring Statement -   See our guidance for writing a reflective teaching statement . Publications -   Up to three key publications Reference requirements 3-5 required (contact information only) Apply link: https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10408 About UC Irvine The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected categories covered by the UC anti-discrimination policy . As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct. “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment or discrimination, as defined by the employer. UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, Students and Third Parties APM - 035: Affirmative Action and Nondiscrimination in Employment . As a University employee, you will be required to comply with all applicable University policies and/or collective bargaining agreements, as may be amended from time to time. Federal, state, or local government directives may impose additional requirements. Job location Irvine, CA Apply now to Assistant Professor (Tenure-Track) Position in Quantum and Semiconductor Engineering or Log in to your portfolio Need help? Contact the hiring department . The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. You have the right to an equal employment opportunity . The University of California, Irvine is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities . See our Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act Annual Security Reports Academic Personnel Recruit University of California, Irvine UC Irvine Accessibility About California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Opt-Out Icon Privacy Policy © 2007-2026 The Regents of the University of California. All rights reserved."
