    "https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10430": {
      "title": "Lecturer",
      "description": "Lecturer - General Chemistry or Organic Chemistry 2026-27 (JPF10430) - UCI - Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Lecturer - General Chemistry or Organic Chemistry 2026-27 (JPF10430) Lecturer - General Chemistry or Organic Chemistry 2026-27 Apply now to Lecturer - General Chemistry or Organic Chemistry 2026-27 Job #JPF10430 Chemistry / School of Physical Sciences / UC Irvine Position overview Salary range: $70,977-$199,722 Application Window Open date: September 8, 2026 Next review date: Friday, Oct 9, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Apply by this date to ensure full consideration by the committee. Final date: Wednesday, Jun 30, 2027 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date, but those received after the review date will only be considered if the position has not yet been filled. Position description The Department of Chemistry anticipates possible positions for Lecturers in General Chemistry and Organic Chemistry for the 2026-27 Academic Year. The percentage of time is variable, depending on the course(s) assigned. The salary is commensurate with experience. This is a temporary position, and the successful candidate(s) will be hired only for the duration of one or more academic quarters in 2026-27 or in the summer session of 2027. Requirements: The minimum requirements are in Ph.D. in Chemistry and an excellent teaching record. Please apply online at with a curriculum vitae including publications list, teaching evaluations (if available), and names of three letters of references (please do not solicit letters). Department : https://www.chem.uci.edu/employment Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) Applications are sought from candidates with Ph.D. degree in Chemistry with an excellent teaching record and large course instruction experience. Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter Statement of Research (Optional) Teaching Statement -   See our guidance for writing a reflective teaching statement . (Optional) Reference requirements 3-5 required (contact information only) Apply link: https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10430 About UC Irvine The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected categories covered by the UC anti-discrimination policy . As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct. “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment or discrimination, as defined by the employer. UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, Students and Third Parties APM - 035: Affirmative Action and Nondiscrimination in Employment . As a University employee, you will be required to comply with all applicable University policies and/or collective bargaining agreements, as may be amended from time to time. Federal, state, or local government directives may impose additional requirements. Job location Irvine, CA Apply now to Lecturer - General Chemistry or Organic Chemistry 2026-27 or Log in to your portfolio Need help? Contact the hiring department . The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. You have the right to an equal employment opportunity . The University of California, Irvine is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities . See our Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act Annual Security Reports Academic Personnel Recruit University of California, Irvine UC Irvine Accessibility About California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Opt-Out Icon Privacy Policy © 2007-2026 The Regents of the University of California. All rights reserved."
    },
    "https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10432": {
      "title": "Part-time limited term Junior Specialist Researcher (JPF10432)",
      "description": "Part-time limited term Junior Specialist Researcher (JPF10432) - UCI - Recruit Skip to main content Recruit Home Open Recruitments Part-time limited term Junior Specialist Researcher (JPF10432) Part-time limited term Junior Specialist Researcher Apply now to Part-time limited term Junior Specialist Researcher Job #JPF10432 Dance / Claire Trevor School of the Arts / UC Irvine Position overview Salary range: $27.30/hr Application Window Open date: September 5, 2026 Next review date: Monday, Oct 5, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Apply by this date to ensure full consideration by the committee. Final date: Monday, Oct 5, 2026 at 11:59pm (Pacific Time) Applications will continue to be accepted until this date. Position description The Dance Department at The Claire Trevor School of the Arts seeks applications for a 6-month part-time limited term researcher in the Junior Specialist series. We seek a highly motivated and knowledgeable individual to assist Professor Kelli Sharp’s laboratory to aid in dance science human movement research. The laboratory focuses on the intersection of dance and science for performing artists and various neurodivergent populations. The appointment is at 30% (hours variable per week; up to 12 hours per week) from October 15, 2026, through April 1, 2027, with the possibility of an extension. A grant-funded position, the budgeted pay rate for this position is $27.30 per hour. Major Job Responsibilities • IRB management • Data collection and data management • Perform literature searches • Assists PI on manuscript development • Assist PI on basic laboratory organization Qualifications Candidate must have at least a BFA, or BS, in dance or exercise physiology (or equivalent). Candidate should be familiar with a wide range of technical skills with working knowledge of various data collection methods used in movement-based human research. Candidate should have good organizational and time management skills. A familiarity with motion capture data collection methods is an asset. Application Requirements ● Curriculum Vitae ● Cover letter ● 3 References Department : http://dance.arts.uci.edu/ Qualifications Basic qualifications (required at time of application) Candidate must have at least a BFA, or BS, in dance or exercise physiology (or equivalent). Candidate should be familiar with a wide range of technical skills with working knowledge of various data collection methods used in movement-based human research. Candidate should have good organizational and time management skills. Application Requirements Document requirements Curriculum Vitae -   Your most recently updated C.V. Cover Letter Statement of Research (Optional) Teaching Statement -   See our guidance for writing a reflective teaching statement . (Optional) Reference requirements 3-5 required (contact information only) Apply link: https://recruit.ap.uci.edu/JPF10432 About UC Irvine The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, age, protected veteran status, or other protected categories covered by the UC anti-discrimination policy . As a condition of employment, the finalist will be required to disclose if they are subject to any final administrative or judicial decisions within the last seven years determining that they committed any misconduct. “Misconduct” means any violation of the policies or laws governing conduct at the applicant’s previous place of employment, including, but not limited to, violations of policies or laws prohibiting sexual harassment, sexual assault, or other forms of harassment or discrimination, as defined by the employer. UC Sexual Violence and Sexual Harassment Policy UC Anti-Discrimination Policy for Employees, Students and Third Parties APM - 035: Affirmative Action and Nondiscrimination in Employment . As a University employee, you will be required to comply with all applicable University policies and/or collective bargaining agreements, as may be amended from time to time. Federal, state, or local government directives may impose additional requirements. Job location Irvine, CA Apply now to Part-time limited term Junior Specialist Researcher or Log in to your portfolio Need help? Contact the hiring department . The University of California, Irvine is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer. You have the right to an equal employment opportunity . The University of California, Irvine is committed to providing reasonable accommodations to applicants with disabilities . See our Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act Annual Security Reports Academic Personnel Recruit University of California, Irvine UC Irvine Accessibility About California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Opt-Out Icon Privacy Policy © 2007-2026 The Regents of the University of California. All rights reserved."
